 # Delivery / host / extension semantic checkpoint (C0 incomplete)
 
+## Continuation after PR18 checkpoint
+
+The initial checkpoint below is preserved verbatim at `snapshots/pr18-initial/`.
+Its statement that pinned external code was unavailable is **superseded**: exact
+`openclaw@2026.9.5`, `@openclaw/discord@2026.9.5`, `@openclaw/acpx@2026.9.5`
+and ACPX's exact dependency `acpx@0.16.0` have been downloaded read-only from
+the npm registry. Registry SHA512 integrity and SHA1 were verified; SHA256 and
+distribution metadata are retained in acquisition records. No package/lifecycle
+scripts were executed and no dependencies installed. Selected full pinned source
+files beneath `pinned-*` and raw excerpts permit review without `/tmp` continuity.
+This establishes code-based definitions, not OCI-image byte equality or runtime
+implementation acceptance.
+
+`refine-pinned-openclaw.py` refines 68 authored Gateway policy fields from actual
+pinned validators **and productive consumers**, adds the actual native
+`agents.defaults.timeoutSeconds` reader/default row, and classifies the one
+schema-declared but inert `channels.discord.inboundWorker.runTimeoutMs` field.
+The collector invokes this refinement when acquisition records are present.
+
+Concrete new source findings:
+
+- Thinking supports `off|minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh|adaptive|max|ultra`; reasoning
+  supports `off|on|stream`. Directive/session/agent/model/default precedence and
+  actual runtime capabilities/authorization still constrain effect. Schema
+  support does not prove a particular model/runtime supports a chosen parameter.
+- `contextPruning.ttl` is schema-string only; invalid duration errors are caught
+  and silently retain a five-minute resolver baseline. Pruning requires eligible
+  **embedded** runtime/provider. Compaction token settings similarly have embedded
+  settings-manager consumers; their presence does not prove effects on model
+  routes pinned to Codex. Explicit `strict-agentic` is inert off the supported
+  OpenAI GPT-5 embedded lane rather than being rejected.
+- Real embedding `openai-compatible` is a core adapter. It requires nonempty
+  endpoint and model; the requested `gemini-embedding-001` is transmitted to the
+  compatible endpoint, not inferred to be a native Gemini route. Remote model
+  availability remains a live service contract, not a local schema guarantee.
+- Chart JSON `gateway.bind=loopback` loses to the current Chart command's
+  `--bind lan`; native CLI gives `opts.bind` precedence. `gateway.tools.allow`
+  removes named default HTTP denies; it is **not** a restrictive universal tool
+  allowlist. Owner-only restrictions and profile/tool deny policies remain.
+- Final ACP backend `allowedAgents` policy compares normalized exact ids and
+  empty permits all; the spawn target-enumeration helper's wildcard handling
+  differs. Both boundaries are retained in the row, not averaged together.
+- Native agent timeout default is **172800 seconds (48 hours)**, not the Chart's
+  inert Discord `inboundWorker.runTimeoutMs=43200000`. Complete recursive exact
+  distribution search found the latter only in schema/type metadata. The target
+  disposition proposes removing this inert key in C3; a new consumer would need
+  separate justified approval. Actual native timeout has override-milliseconds,
+  override-seconds, config, then literal precedence and timer-safe zero sentinel.
+- Thread-binding expiry/feature policy has account > channel > global defaults
+  and stored lifecycle implications. Subagent run timeout is stored separately;
+  archive cleanup can consult current config. These are R/S identity/deadline
+  contracts, not automatically next-module changes.
+
+Evidence: `openclaw-pinned-observations.json`, acquisition JSON records,
+`pinned-unused-inbound-worker-search.json`, exact full source snapshots and current
+inventory rows. Remaining Chart/script/native implicit policy obligations are
+still open. No global C0 completion, runtime PASS or C1 approval is claimed.
+
